,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":false,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":0.0,"_gate_accruals":-0.05123658422771815,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":50.6,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.3421888532958599,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":16.5,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.07861039054801935,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":1.7,"_gate_piotroski":3,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":33.3,"_gate_spread":-0.07721484825740196,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":3.871044277977479,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.21146694562377857,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.06647341041326273,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":11.2,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.01989803781084576,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":34.9,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.5712242829827476,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.00890978873967751,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":58.9,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04873531468509657,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":65.3,"_gate_share_shrink":0.00028192843499996734,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":49.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.009439200444197668,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":84.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.0137600005,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":9.2,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Newell Brands Inc. engages in the design, manufacture, sourcing, and distribution of consumer and commercial products worldwide. The company operates in three segments: Home and Commercial Solutions, Learning and Development, and Outdoor and Recreation. The Commercial Solutions segment provides commercial cleaning and maintenance solution products under the Rubbermaid, Rubbermaid Commercial Products, Mapa, and Spontex brands; closet and garage organization products; hygiene systems and material handling solutions; household products, such as kitchen appliances under the Crockpot, Mr. Coffee, Oster, and Sunbeam brands; small appliances under the Breville brand name in Europe; food and home storage products under the FoodSaver, Rubbermaid, Ball, and Sistema brands; fresh preserving products; vacuum sealing products; and gourmet cookware, bakeware, and cutlery under the Calphalon brand; and home fragrance products under the Chesapeake Bay, WoodWick, and Yankee Candle brands. The Learning and Development segment offers writing instruments, including markers and highlighters, pens, and pencils; art products; activity-based products; labeling solutions; and baby gear and infant care products under the Dymo, Elmer's, EXPO, Graco, NUK, Paper Mate, Parker, and Sharpie brands. The Outdoor and Recreation segment provides outdoor and outdoor-related products, inlcuding technical apparel and on-the-go beverageware under the Bubba, Campingaz, Coleman, Contigo, and Marmot brands. It serves large mass merchandisers, discount stores, home centers, warehouse clubs, office superstores, direct-to-consumer channels, specialty retailers and wholesalers, commercial distributors and e-commerce retailers, grocery stores, and sporting goods, as well as direct to consumers online, select contract customers, and other professional customers. The company was founded in 1903 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christopher H. Peterson | President, CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $3.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 21K people. Revenue per employee of $329K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Defensive peers. Each employee generates $776 of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Newell Brands Inc. is a mid-cap consumer defensive business with a $2.5B market cap on $7.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -9% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 34%.","The business throws off $17M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 0 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 12.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 196% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 10% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Netwealth Group (ASX:NWL) Shares in Focus: Why Is the ASX 200 Stock on the Radar?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/midcap/netwealth-group-asxnwl-shares-in-focus-why-is-the-asx-200-stock-on-the-radar","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794571920.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.077,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Netwealth Group (ASX:NWL) Shares in Focus: Why Is the ASX 200 Stock Drawing Attention?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/midcap/netwealth-group-asxnwl-shares-in-focus-why-is-the-asx-200-stock-drawing-attention","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794571860.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.743,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Netwealth (ASX:NWL): Service Quality Remains Its Adviser Edge","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/retirement-planning/netwealth-asxnwl-service-quality-remains-its-adviser-edge","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794564360.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.052,"t